{"name":"Vodka","hex":"#bfc0ee","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Vodka","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of vodka (“Russian”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Vodka"}],"entries":[{"title":"Vodka","blocks":[{"text":"Vodka is a clear distilled alcoholic beverage. Its varieties originated in Poland and Russia. Vodka is composed mainly of water and ethanol (alcohol), sometimes with traces of impurities and flavourings. Traditionally it is made by distilling liquid from fermented cereal grains and potatoes since the latter was introduced in Europe in the 18th century. Some modern brands use maize, sugar cane, fruit, honey, or maple sap as the base."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Smirnoff_Red_Label_8213.jpg/330px-Smirnoff_Red_Label_8213.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vodka"},{"title":"Vodka (horse)","blocks":[{"text":"Vodka  was a Japanese Thoroughbred racehorse and broodmare. She won seven G1 races in Japan, including the 2007 Tokyo Yūshun, the first filly to win this race in 64 years since Kurifuji in 1943 as well as the 2009 Japan Cup. She was awarded the JRA Horse of the Year award in 2008 and 2009 and was inducted to the Japan Racing Association Hall of Fame in 2011."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Vodka%28horse%29_20070527R1.jpg/330px-Vodka%28horse%29_20070527R1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vodka_(horse)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/VodkaBelt.png/500px-VodkaBelt.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/VodkaBelt.png/500px-VodkaBelt.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnai